{
 "schema": "sw-ml-study.conversation-script",
 "version": 1,
 "note": "Demo 01's conversation script: the deterministic half of ELIZA. The model chooses a class; this script decides how to answer it from the visitor's own words. Patterns match cleaned words (apostrophes removed, so don't is dont); * matches any run of words; {1}, {2} are the wildcard captures and {all} the whole input, each reflected (my -> your, i -> you); {w} is the word a find rule found. Many reassemblies are Weizenbaum's 1966 DOCTOR script. Nouls: a question is deflected first, as Weizenbaum's program did; when the model cannot decide, a longer input is reflected with its sentiment, and a short one brings back a memory.",
